                  "declaration": "CartLine",
                  "reading": "The author modified a component `<CartLine />` that:\n\n- declares a function `handleRemove()`, which calls `window.confirm()` with `` `Remove ${item.product.name} from your cart?` `` and calls `removeItem(item.product.id)` only when the result is `true`\n- passes `handleRemove` as `onClick` to the Remove `<Button>`, where it passed `() => removeItem(item.product.id)` before\n\nA click on Remove now takes the item out of the cart only after the shopper confirms, so that one click no longer removes an item. A cancel leaves the cart as it is. [`removeItem()`](code:src/stores/cart-store.ts#L16-18) is unchanged: it [keeps every item whose `product.id` is not the id it is given](code:src/stores/cart-store.ts#L17). `<CartPage />` in `src/routes/cart/index.tsx` renders one `<CartLine />` per item with the prop `item`, and `<CartLine />` still takes that prop and no other.",
